n on disk and compares it to the current active FW version on the touch IC and updates it accordingly.  The actual updates are performed using a commandline tool called wacom_update.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:372327 BUG=chromium:624262 TEST=Deployed on a device including a Wacom touchscreen and rebooted, the firmware script updates the firmware when needed and chooses not to when the firmware version is up to date.  Change-Id: If9b22192f66a0dd434fa2030721fa2f4c98f7a49 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/351830 Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="351830" owner_email="tobita.tatsunosuke@wacom.co.jp" pass_count="0" patch_number="35" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" ref="refs/changes/30/351830/35" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Id9749e9dc26498f4ff7f7893e6d152100d49a0c9" commit="c1ec93b140f13eb22dec3166604e1fb3202fcd93" commit_message="UPSTREAM: PCI: rockchip: Add Rockchip PCIe controller support  Add support for the Rockchip PCIe controller found on RK3399 SoC platform.  [bhelgaas: fold in Brian's rockchip_pcie_client_irq_handler() OR fix, other fixes and cleanups from Guenter Roeck &lt;linux@roeck-us.net&gt; and me] Signed-off-by: Shawn Lin &lt;shawn.lin@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Bjorn Helgaas &lt;bhelgaas@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/helgaas/pci.git pci/host-rockchip  commit abe17181b16f24b8e0a5315eb0090cf74efc2a59)  [Brian: synced with upstream; resolved trivial conflicts  Conflicts:  MAINTAINERS  drivers/pci/host/Makefile ]  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56693 TEST=boot kevin; test Wifi  Change-Id: Id9749e9dc26498f4ff7f7893e6d152100d49a0c9 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/376964 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="376964" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/64/376964/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7787eead0c864ba2fe2978bd5679917bef4fa3b2" commit="7eab03d7aa4e78982fafb8a12d7906164a6b245f" commit_message="COMMIT-QUEUE.ini: Fix typo.  I mistakenly had `chell-no-vmtest-only-pre-cq`, but it turns out that's not a valid builder config.  Just need to drop the &quot;only&quot; part.  BUG=chromium:642503 BRANCH=None TEST=`cbuildbot --list --all | grep chell-no-vmtest-pre-cq`  Change-Id: I7787eead0c864ba2fe2978bd5679917bef4fa3b2 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383878 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="383878" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/78/383878/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Id1f0d11012d96afb04b9d872e7527f537c45d282" commit="6ecdc195d29a064037c835ec5dd70513caea09f3" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: remove lock debug configs from arm64  This removes some lock debug configs that were added while ago and renormalizes the configs.  This is the equivalent to:   echo &quot;# CONFIG_PROVE_LOCKING is not set&quot; &gt;&gt;     chromeos/config/arm64/common.config   echo &quot;# CONFIG_DEBUG_LOCK_ALLOC is not set&quot; &gt;&gt;     chromeos/config/arm64/common.config   echo &quot;# CONFIG_DEBUG_MUTEXES is not set&quot; &gt;&gt;     chromeos/config/arm64/common.config   echo &quot;# CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL is not set&quot; &gt;&gt;     chromeos/config/arm64/common.config   ./chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig oldconfig  ...atop an already normalized config.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56441 TEST=modprobe configs; zcat /proc/config.gz | grep PROVE  Change-Id: Id1f0d11012d96afb04b9d872e7527f537c45d282 Signed-off-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/374701 " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="374701" owner_email="dbasehore@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/01/374701/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2f94c7172a80578823254f5fd486aa7104f35387" commit="ba019d4e947de9237a61439500684397b72cb63d" commit_message="servo v2: Set dut_hub_pwren init to be on.  In autotest during servo init, the dut_hub_pwren control is explicity set to 'on' and never touched afterwards.  In servo v3, dut_hub_pwren control already has the init set to 'on' and in servo v4, there does not exist a dut_hub_pwren signal (the closest is dut_usb_hub_reset).  To avoid the need to create a fake dut_hub_pwren for servo v4, let's have the init set it to 'on' for servo v2 and take out the code in autotest that toggles dut_hub_pwren.  BUG=None TEST=Test that firmware_FAFTSetup still works on a servo v2 and gnawty.  Change-Id: I2f94c7172a80578823254f5fd486aa7104f35387 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383672 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt